---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'September 9, 2026';
---

<Layout
	title="Terms & Conditions — GFR Calculator"
	description="Terms and conditions for using GFR Calculator, the free online eGFR and kidney function calculator."
>
	<article class="container-page py-14 sm:py-20">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
			<p class="font-mono text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-mute">Terms &amp; Conditions</p>
			<h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
			<p class="mt-4 text-sm text-faint">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

			<p class="mt-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				By accessing or using gfrcalc.com (the "Site"), you agree to these Terms &amp; Conditions.
				If you do not agree, please do not use the Site.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Not medical advice</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				The Site provides an educational calculator that estimates glomerular filtration rate
				(eGFR) using published formulas (CKD-EPI 2021, CKD-EPI 2009, MDRD, and Cockcroft-Gault).
				Results are estimates only and are <strong>not</strong> a medical diagnosis, a substitute
				for professional medical advice, or a basis for treatment decisions. Always consult a
				qualified healthcare professional regarding your kidney function or any medical condition.
				See our <a href="/methodology" class="text-link hover:text-link-deep">methodology</a> page
				for formula sources and limitations.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">No warranty</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				The Site and its calculators are provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties
				of any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to accuracy, completeness,
				reliability, or fitness for a particular purpose. While we test our formulas against
				published reference values, we do not guarantee that results will be error-free or
				suitable for any specific clinical use.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Limitation of liability</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				To the fullest extent permitted by law, GFR Calculator and its operators shall not be
				liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from your
				use of, or inability to use, the Site or any calculator results, including any decisions
				made based on those results.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Acceptable use</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				You agree not to misuse the Site, including by attempting to disrupt its operation,
				scraping it in a manner that degrades service for other users, or using it for any
				unlawful purpose.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Intellectual property</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				The Site's design, text, and code are owned by GFR Calculator or its licensors unless
				otherwise noted. The underlying clinical formulas (CKD-EPI, MDRD, Cockcroft-Gault) are
				published, publicly available equations and are not proprietary to this Site.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Changes to these terms</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				We may revise these Terms &amp; Conditions at any time. Continued use of the Site after
				changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Privacy</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				Please also review our <a href="/privacy-policy" class="text-link hover:text-link-deep">Privacy Policy</a>,
				which explains how we handle data on the Site.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Contact us</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				Questions about these terms can be sent through our
				<a href="/contact" class="text-link hover:text-link-deep">Contact Us</a> page.
			</p>
		</div>
	</article>
</Layout>
